The one design decision worth explaining: the C program hands out two aliasing raw pointers — one to [38;5;10mmain[0m's automatic [38;5;10minitial_value[0m, one to [38;5;10mstatic_alias[0m's function-local [38;5;10mstatic int inner[0m. Rather than reproduce that with raw pointers, I keep both integers as fields of a [38;5;10mState[0m struct and model the pointer as a two-variant tag ([38;5;10mRef::Outer[0m / [38;5;10mRef::Inner[0m). That makes the program's real quirk explicit: once [38;5;10mstatic_alias[0m returns [38;5;10m&inner[0m, the next call passes [38;5;10m&inner[0m in as [38;5;10mouter[0m, so [38;5;10m*outer >= inner[0m compares the variable against itself (always true) and [38;5;10minner += *outer[0m becomes [38;5;10minner += inner[0m. The sum doubles every iteration from then on and never returns to the outer variable — [38;5;10mdriver 7 5[0m prints 8, 16, 32, 64, 128.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
Behaviors preserved deliberately rather than fixed:[0m[0m
[0m[0m
- Error messages go to stdout via [38;5;10mprintf[0m, not stderr, and exit with status 1 in the original check order.[0m[0m
- [38;5;10mstrtol[0m is reimplemented over raw argument bytes: C-locale whitespace skipping, optional sign, base-10 only (so [38;5;10m0x10[0m parses as [38;5;10m0[0m), trailing garbage accepted ([38;5;10m12abc[0m → 12), and saturation to [38;5;10mLONG_MAX[0m/[38;5;10mLONG_MIN[0m on range errors. The [38;5;10mlong[0m→[38;5;10mint[0m narrowing is then a wrapping cast, which is why [38;5;10m2147483648[0m behaves as it does in both binaries.[0m[0m
- Signed overflow in the accumulator is UB in C but wraps in practice under gcc [38;5;10m-O2[0m; I used [38;5;10mwrapping_add[0m to match. The doubling chain reaching 0 is confirmed identical in both.[0m[0m
- Only the count of [38;5;10margc != 3[0m is checked, and [38;5;10margs_os[0m is used so non-UTF-8 arguments don't panic.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
One caveat on scope: the C program reads nothing from stdin, so the stdin-behavior requirement in your instructions doesn't apply here — there are no [38;5;10mscanf[0m/[38;5;10mfgets[0m calls to mirror. Equivalence was established against gcc [38;5;10m-O2[0m on this Linux host; since the overflow paths are UB in C, a different compiler or optimization level could in principle diverge from the reference I tested against.[0m[0m
